From: Luke Johnson <jaewun@me.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: keep icc WAKE-TCS floor in d3cold suspend (SM8550 CXPC wake)

The d3cold suspend path fully icc_disable()s the ALWAYS-tagged pcie-mem/
cpu-pcie interconnect, which zeros their WAKE TCS votes. On SM8550 the AOP
then sees an insufficient vote at wake and the SoC never resumes from CXPC.
Keep the kBps_to_icc(1) keep-alive floor (as the non-d3cold path does).
---
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -2150,13 +2150,20 @@
 		return ret;
 
 	if (pcie->pci->suspended) {
-		ret = icc_disable(pcie->icc_mem);
+		/*
+		 * AYN Thor: icc_disable() here zeros the ALWAYS-tagged pcie-mem /
+		 * cpu-pcie WAKE TCS vote, so the AOP sees an insufficient vote at
+		 * wake and the SoC never resumes from CXPC. Keep the kBps_to_icc(1)
+		 * keep-alive floor (as the non-d3cold path does) so the WAKE TCS
+		 * entry stays non-zero.
+		 */
+		ret = icc_set_bw(pcie->icc_mem, 0, kBps_to_icc(1));
 		if (ret)
-			dev_err(dev, "Failed to disable PCIe-MEM interconnect path: %d\n", ret);
+			dev_err(dev, "Failed to floor PCIe-MEM interconnect path: %d\n", ret);
 
-		ret = icc_disable(pcie->icc_cpu);
+		ret = icc_set_bw(pcie->icc_cpu, 0, kBps_to_icc(1));
 		if (ret)
-			dev_err(dev, "Failed to disable CPU-PCIe interconnect path: %d\n", ret);
+			dev_err(dev, "Failed to floor CPU-PCIe interconnect path: %d\n", ret);
 
 		if (pcie->use_pm_opp)
 			dev_pm_opp_set_opp(pcie->pci->dev, NULL);
